      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The challenge of a chemical approach to the origins of life problem involves comprehending the transition from prebiotic chemistry to protobiology. This endeavor demands demonstrating the metamorphosis of a diverse pool of prebiotic building blocks (heterogeneous heterogeneity) into a conglomerate self-assembling system (homogeneous heterogeneity) capable of evolution."},
